:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.21.1</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated Vanilla to 0.5.12.11</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated DoLP to v0.778</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated RBE to v0.6.1</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Autism Spectrum: diagnosis, disclosure, and daily life</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Noise, bright light, crowds, and stressful demands now build <strong>Load</strong>, leaving the player Settled, Strained, or Burnt Out depending on their current state.</li>
		<li>Maximum Load depends on Willpower.</li>
		<li>Sleep, quiet time, stimming, and spending time on the current fixation reduce Load, each with its own daily limit.</li>
		<li><strong>Masking</strong> now tracks the effort of acting as others expect. It builds faster around strangers, slower around people who know the player is autistic, and not at all around people they fully trust.</li>
		<li>Keeping the mask up costs energy, while dropping it somewhere safe helps recovery.</li>
		<li>The player can practise masking in a mirror for a temporary benefit.</li>
		<li>Autistic characters can have difficulty starting tasks, affecting lessons, chores, jobs, training, and community service.</li>
		<li>Unresolved problems such as rent, suspension, and community service can add daily Stress.</li>
		<li>Added a full autism diagnosis route through Harper, including developmental history and supporting evidence.</li>
		<li>The free waiting-list route takes several months, while a £1,500 private assessment is much faster.</li>
		<li>The player can switch from the free route to private assessment at any time.</li>
		<li>After diagnosis, the player chooses who can access the report, including the school office, nurse, individual teachers, Bailey, or nobody.</li>
		<li>Robin, Kylar, Whitney, Sydney, Eden, Avery, Alex, Leighton, Bailey, and teachers can react differently based on the player's state and relationship with them.</li>
		<li><strong>Stimming</strong> can now be used anywhere in a safe zone.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new “enemies with benefits” content for Whitney</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Defeating Whitney in combat once permanently unlocks new eager, consensual options.</li>
		<li>These can appear during street make-outs and fondling, public oral scenes, milkshake escalation, and post-rescue reward scenes.</li>
		<li>Requires Promiscuity 4–5.</li>
		<li>Public options also require Exhibitionism 3–4, while private options do not.</li>
		<li>These choices increase Arousal and Whitney's Lust without increasing Dominance, Submission, Stress, or Trauma.</li>
		<li>Make-out scenes now have unique text showing the player genuinely enjoying them.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more Poppy content</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Poppy can now visit the park, walk around town, and appear in repeatable park and street encounters.</li>
		<li>The player can invite Poppy on park or cafe dates from their flat.</li>
		<li>Street, park, cafe, and scheduled park scenes now include more activities, conversations, choices, affection, and endings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added the Underground Colosseum</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added an illegal fighting arena beneath an old factory in the industrial alleyways.</li>
		<li>The player can discover it through rumours, get the passphrase from Landry, and find the entrance behind a skip.</li>
		<li><strong>Extended combat</strong> must be enabled to enter.</li>
		<li>Fight naked before a paying crowd and rise from F to S rank.</li>
		<li>The player begins as unknown <strong>meat</strong>, but can earn an arena name after enough fights.</li>
		<li>Higher ranks introduce faster opponents and make blocking, countering, feinting, and hook punches more important.</li>
		<li>Up to three fights can be entered per day, with extra risk on the third bout.</li>
		<li>Losing can cause injuries lasting several days, with visible injuries affecting reactions around town, school, and Bailey.</li>
		<li>The arena includes bookmakers, a fighters' bar, locker rooms, showers, a mirror, and a private gallery.</li>
		<li>The player can bet on other fights or themselves, with daily limits for fighters.</li>
		<li>Match-fixing offers can appear, with consequences for failing to throw the fight.</li>
		<li>Arena debt can attract collectors.</li>
		<li>Successful fighters can eventually receive a champion offer from the gallery.</li>
		<li>The player can cooperate, steal the arena's records, refuse them, or free the indebted fighters held downstairs.</li>
		<li>Freeing the fighters permanently closes the Colosseum and puts the arena's people on the streets until enough have been dealt with.</li>
		<li>Combat Fame can reach 4,000 through the Colosseum. Other sources remain capped at 2,000.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a mirror to the office agency</strong>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Optimised sidebar sky performance</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The animated sidebar weather sky now redraws only when needed, reuses its canvas, and shares a single animation loop.</li>
		<li>Hidden title-screen sky animations stop after leaving the title screen.</li>
		<li>Turning off <strong>Use new weather renderer for sidebar</strong> now fully disables the renderer.</li>
		<li>Fixed invisible title-screen rendering, weather effects running too slowly, and an unused rain mask.</li>
		<li>No save data is affected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Split Ear Slime settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Ear Slimes now have their own toggle separate from normal Slimes.</li>
		<li>Existing saves copy the current Slime setting to both options so behaviour stays unchanged until the player edits the new setting.</li>
		<li>Imported older settings now carry over correctly.</li>
		<li>Whitney can no longer give a slime while Slimes are disabled; they use an urchin instead, or skip the rear parasite when anal content is disabled.</li>
		<li>Sewer Slimes can no longer attach to the clitoris while Parasites are disabled.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Autism Spectrum Load recovery</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sleeping no longer consumes the daily Load recovery limit.</li>
		<li>Calm time at 0 Load no longer consumes the limit either.</li>
		<li>Daytime recovery from rest, quiet time, and focused interests remains available.</li>
		<li>Daily Load recovery increased from 12 to 15.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated combat stat gains</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Deviancy can now increase during non-consensual beast encounters while in Rut, Heat, or under Hypnotic Deviancy.</li>
		<li>Reverse rape grants Deviancy against beasts and Promiscuity against humans.</li>
		<li>Normal non-consensual human encounters still grant neither.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Hyper Fertility speeds up pregnancies again</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Pregnancies affected by Hyper Fertility once again progress at <strong>6× normal speed</strong>.</li>
		<li>If Beta gives the player a second womb, both pregnancies speed up together.</li>
		<li>Conception boosts and multiple births are unchanged.</li>
		<li>Labour that has already started keeps its normal timing.</li>
		<li>Existing saves need no repair and start progressing correctly from the next day.</li>
		<li>The tooltip now explicitly says it also speeds up parasite and non-humanoid pregnancies.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated relationship pet names</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Partners and friends no longer guess the player's gender from clothing.</li>
		<li>Characters who know the player use what they know about the player's identity when choosing words such as boyfriend or girlfriend.</li>
		<li>Whitney, Kylar, Avery, Sydney, Poppy, Gwylan, and Robin now follow this behaviour.</li>
		<li>Strangers and bullies still judge by appearance.</li>
		<li>The player's own dialogue follows their pronouns.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Transgender characters now start with matching Identity defaults</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Choosing Transgender now sets appearance, clothing, pronoun, and genital preferences opposite to the starting body by default.</li>
		<li>Birth-sex options are marked as unaccepted so misgendering can cause Dysphoria as intended.</li>
		<li>Manual choices on the Identity screen still override these defaults.</li>
		<li>Existing saves are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Kylar and other NPCs no longer get angry when protection is already unwanted</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Removing an NPC's condom or locking their legs no longer causes Anger or Trust loss when that NPC already does not want protection.</li>
		<li>Applies to Kylar, Eden, Black Wolf, Gwylan, Great Hawk, Ivory Wraith, and monogamous Bailey.</li>
		<li>Normal Defiance and Stress relief still apply.</li>
		<li>Kylar has unique dialogue for both actions, including removing one of their sabotaged condoms.</li>
		<li>Kylar and Robin will not force chastity on the player again.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gender Identity and pronoun tracking</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Disabling <strong>Update Gender Identity from your Identity system</strong> now fully freezes the Gender Identity meter.</li>
		<li>Older saves no longer change the meter during load when the setting is disabled.</li>
		<li>New games still start with a meter matching the player's Identity choices.</li>
		<li>Missing meters repair automatically.</li>
		<li>Re-enabling automatic updates resumes gradual changes from the current value instead of resetting it.</li>
		<li>Masculine, feminine, and neutral pronoun use is tracked correctly so pronoun tolerance can increase as intended.</li>
		<li>Pronouns used during flashbacks, dreams, and replays are no longer recorded.</li>
		<li>Temporary pronoun tracking clears correctly each hour.</li>
		<li>Event-driven Gender Identity changes remain separate from daily drift.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Ivory Wraith bodywriting settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Can overwrite existing tattoos</strong> and <strong>Even during nightmares</strong> are now correctly disabled when supernatural bodywriting is turned off.</li>
		<li>Fixed the tattoo-bypass checkbox.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gentleman's Club letters going missing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Letters are now sent to the room where the player currently sleeps instead of an unavailable former home.</li>
		<li>Existing saves repair themselves on load.</li>
		<li>Waiting letters can be collected again.</li>
		<li>The sidebar notice appears only on the delivery day, while the Journal continues to show unread letters.</li>
		<li>Bailey no longer tells the player to ask Avery for food before Avery has been met.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed daily events and stats getting stuck</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Saves stuck in a dream, vision, or flashback state now repair once the player returns to a normal area.</li>
		<li>Daily and hourly updates resume normally.</li>
		<li>The player's real body and stats are restored.</li>
		<li>This fixes daily events remaining permanently used and stats such as Innocence and Awareness no longer changing.</li>
		<li>Affected saves repair automatically.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Exhibitionist Fame and combat soft caps</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Exhibitionist now correctly reduces Exhibition Fame gains by 75%, including exposed dancing.</li>
		<li>The old check incorrectly used the Nerd background.</li>
		<li>Promiscuity and Deviancy can continue gaining slowly in combat after reaching their rank soft caps, matching non-combat behaviour.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Innocence bypassing lewdness checks</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The Innocence bonus now weakens properly as Awareness rises toward zero.</li>
		<li>The bonus disappears completely when Innocence ends.</li>
		<li>The Characteristics overlay no longer says <strong>You are innocent</strong> when the trait is inactive.</li>
		<li>The Innocence meter no longer tries to render a negative bar width.</li>
		<li>Ending Innocence safely restores Trauma even if none was stored beforehand.</li>
		<li>Fixed one X-Change pill route failing to clear stored Trauma after restoration.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed stored cum and pregnancy Dysphoria</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Scoop out</strong> now detects and removes both visible fluid and stored vaginal/anal cum loads.</li>
		<li>Works in the home bathroom, cabin, park toilets, and school toilets.</li>
		<li>Dildo and butt-plug removal and reinsertion are unchanged.</li>
		<li>Bathing still removes only washable fluid, while scooping can remove deeper stored loads.</li>
		<li>Stored viable cum no longer triggers pregnancy Dysphoria every hour.</li>
		<li>Creampies still trigger their normal immediate Dysphoria reaction.</li>
		<li>Known pregnancies continue to cause hourly Dysphoria normally.</li>
		<li>Fixed orgasm cleanup after <strong>Scoop Out Vagina/Anus</strong> in school and park toilets.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan sex, chastity, and clothing requests</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan's penis now stays synchronised with the correct vagina, anus, or mouth target during purging sex.</li>
		<li>The previous oral action no longer appears incorrectly while riding.</li>
		<li>Gwylan is excluded from the generic angry-opponent chastity punishment and will not force a device or steal its key.</li>
		<li>One-piece clothing requests no longer become impossible because hidden outfit parts inherit unsupported colour requirements.</li>
		<li>Existing affected requests should work correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery misreading wrong-way pills</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery now separates Gender Identity from physical sex.</li>
		<li>Dialogue can recognise nonbinary characters while forced-pill logic continues to use physical sex.</li>
		<li>If a pill has already changed the player into Avery's sex, Avery now tells them to reverse it or wait for it to wear off instead of blaming clothing.</li>
		<li>Updated date invitation and pre-date checks.</li>
		<li>Fixed nearby grammar errors.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin cafe issues</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed broken pronouns in Robin cafe milk scenes.</li>
		<li>Robin now actually leaves their room and works at the Ocean Breeze from 5–7 PM.</li>
		<li>A note appears on their door during the shift.</li>
		<li>Robin goes directly to work instead of stopping for a bath first.</li>
		<li>Talking to Robin at the cafe no longer opens an empty page with only a <strong>Next</strong> link.</li>
		<li>The shift ends correctly at 7 PM.</li>
		<li>Robin drinking the player's milk now drains it instead of refilling it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed encounters ending without a climax</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Scenes ending because of alarms, passing out, timers, or other interruptions no longer leave a broken leftover <strong>Next</strong> link.</li>
		<li>Alleyways Rescue Fight and Kylar's park streak no longer show <strong>You can't take it anymore</strong> every turn.</li>
		<li>Give-up links now appear only when the player actually gives up.</li>
		<li>79 scenes were fixed.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed fame propagation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fame propagation no longer crashes the daily blackmail update or applies duplicate Fame penalties.</li>
		<li>Stored identities now respect normal Fame limits.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey card-game docks detour</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The first eligible Bailey win always triggers the docks detour.</li>
		<li>Repeat eligible wins have a 34% chance to use the docks route.</li>
		<li>Other wins continue to use the Reiyu's <strong>Drive Home</strong> scene.</li>
		<li>The Intimidate option is unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Temple quest travel issues</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed the pirate ship getting stuck at sea, including already-affected saves.</li>
		<li>Starting a new voyage resets stale journey state.</li>
		<li>Visiting the Pirate Deck repairs a stuck voyage automatically.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed cheat menu</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed Bird Tower bonfire upgrades not applying correctly through <strong>Quick-Complete Tower</strong>.</li>
		<li>Reusing Quick-Complete updates the firepit to the correct burn time, cooking speed, and rack capacity.</li>
		<li>Fixed island teleport cleanup missing many island passages.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon crossing counters now reset correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pronoun errors</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sydney's corrupt nightmare no longer fills the page with undefined-pronoun errors.</li>
		<li>Pronouns are now checked throughout each part of the dream.</li>
		<li>Fixed Avery's drinks-cabinet warning showing pronoun errors while Avery was away.</li>
		<li>Fixed Avery handing the player a drink “himself” regardless of Avery's pronouns.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed wardrobe delivery and MMA storage</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Automatically replaced clothes are no longer sent to inaccessible lockers.</li>
		<li>Replacements now go only to wardrobes that accept deliveries, with the orphanage as fallback.</li>
		<li>Added a proper locker to the MMA gym changing room for storing gym clothing.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed realistic childbirth and Water Dragon egg births</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed incorrect seasonal weather</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed missing NPC in the pub pop quiz &amp; police bribe</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed tooltip behaviour again</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Danube Meal</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change combat pill text</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Anal pill insertion now has unique aftermath text.</li>
		<li>It no longer uses swallowing or bitter-taste lines.</li>
		<li>Applies to no-effect pills, normal pills, and spiked pills with or without side effects.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
